ib/container_server_test.go and container_server_test_inject.go -- directly track the StorageImageServer/StorageRuntimeServer signature change. Related.\n  * server/container_create_linux_test.go -- pure arity adaptation for addOCIBindMounts(..., nil); REQUIRED for the server package's tests to compile, even though the RRO assertions themselves are unrelated.\n  * server/container_events_test.go -- from sub-commit e02bb25aa ('server: fix race in ContainerEvents two-client test') inside the merge. Technically a separate flake fix, but it is a real race fix the pipeline's full-suite gate can trip on; keep it (a redundant port costs time, a missing one costs correctness).\n\nTARGET PREREQUISITES: none mandatory. All vendored deps (image/v5 signature, oci/layout with layout.List, image.UnparsedInstanceWithReference, blobinfocache/none, common/libimage CopyOptions.RemoveSignatures, common/pkg/libartifact ArtifactStore.List/Remove + NewArtifactStorageReference + ArtifactList, json-iterator) are vendored on release-1.35, and pkg/config keeps the same import path plus RuntimePullImage. The single genuine structural gap is internal/ociartifact/datastore (main rewrote it in 99520fec9, target still embeds *ociartifact.Store) -- judged portable:false, i.e. adapt rather than backport, because target's ociartifact.Store already offers List/Remove/RootPath/Pull and identical Reference/CanonicalName/Digest wrappers in internal/ociartifact/artifact.go.\n\nKNOWN BASELINE TEST FAILURE (measured on the pristine target tree a45f7d527, before any change): the full short suite is 37 ok packages + exactly one failure -- server: TestAddOCIBindsRROMountsError/should_fail_to_add_an_RRO_mount_without_private_propagation. It is NOT introduced by this PR and NOT fixable in code: the test case feeds HostPath \"/mnt\" with PROPAGATION_BIDIRECTIONAL and expects the propagation check to reject it first, but addOCIBindMounts runs ensureShared(\"/mnt\") before the RRO/propagation switch; in this container / is an overlay mounted `private` and mount() is denied (no CAP_SYS_ADMIN: CapEff=0x800405fb), so ensureShared returns `got path \"/mnt\" is mounted on \"/\" but it is not a shared mount` and the expected message never appears. The upstream fix does touch this very test function (adds a trailing `nil` argument) and the whole server package, so the agent must still make it compile; the expected-value mismatch itself cannot be resolved by this backport -- it requires either a mount-capable runner (upstream CI runs with `--privileged`/rshared root propagation, e.g. `mount --make-rshared /`) or making /mnt a bind-mounted shared mount in the test environment. Recorded here explicitly so it is not mistaken for a regression of the backport.\n\nDIFFICULTY/RECOMMENDATION: EXTREME (4-level dependency chain, 6 brand-new files, ~2670 lines, two alternative interface implementations, 54 accessor call sites across 18 files, one generated mock, one restructured datastore package) but PROCEED_WITH_CAUTION rather than MANUAL_REVIEW because there are no missing prerequisites, no vendoring changes, no generated/binary blockers, and the adaptation surface is well understood (drop SandboxInfo keying in favour of handler keying, add the four datastore methods against target's Store shape, then mechanically convert every StorageImageServer()/StorageRuntimeServer() call site to the error-returning form)."
